.TH MODBUS-SCRAPER 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-scraper \- Prometheus exporter for Huawei SUN2000 inverters
(Modbus TCP, stdlib only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-scraper
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Prometheus exporter for Huawei SUN2000 inverters (Modbus TCP, stdlib
only). Polls the inverter over Modbus TCP and serves the huawei_* metrics
the dashboard expects at /metrics in the Prometheus text format: the PV
generation, the grid exchange (import/export split), the home consumption
implied by the balance, the battery (optional) and the health gauges
(huawei_up, the error counter, the last poll age).
.PP
Every poll is sanity-checked: a negative PV reading, an array larger than
\fB--max-kwp\fR, a grid line beyond \fB--max-grid-kw\fR or a negative
home balance marks the exposition \fB503\fR (the sensors are suspect, not
the poller) and names the register in the log. A modbus-cache in front of
the device is detected automatically (its synthesized diagnostics block)
and adds the device-up / cache-age / cache-uptime gauges.
.PP
The exposition endpoint is the tool's serving surface: the connection caps
(\fB--max-clients\fR total, \fB--max-conn-per-ip\fR per peer, extras
get an immediate 503), the idle keep-alive kick (\fB--client-timeout\fR)
and the bearer token (\fB--auth-token\fR/\fB--auth-token-file\fR). A
non-loopback listen without a token refuses to start (F13 in
docs/AUDIT.md).
.PP
The JSON-lines control server (\fB--control-port\fR, talked to with
\fBmodbus-scraper-ctl\fR(1) and \fBmodbus-scraper-cli\fR(1)) inspects
and steers the running exporter: the live settings, an immediate poll, the
config reload, the Modbus session restart, the graceful shutdown. With a
control token configured the wire is HMAC-signed: every command and reply
carries the full sha256 of its payload, keyed by the token
(common/wiresec.py) \(em a token-holding client verifies both directions,
and over TCP the signed commands are mandatory.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config
config file (default: $SCRAPER_CONFIG, then scraper.ini next to this
script, then the subproject root) (default:
/Users/oom/GensparkCode/pv\-dash/scrape/scraper.ini)
.TP
.B \-\-host
inverter Modbus TCP address (default: config, $SCRAPER_HOST or
127.0.0.1)
.TP
.BI \-\-modbus\-port " N"
inverter Modbus TCP port (default: config, $SCRAPER_MODBUS_PORT or 5502)
.TP
.BI \-\-unit " N"
Modbus unit id (default: config, $SCRAPER_UNIT or 1)
.TP
.BI \-\-modbus\-offset " N"
added to register addresses (default: config, $SCRAPER_MODBUS_OFFSET or
0)
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
Modbus timeout in seconds (default: config, $SCRAPER_TIMEOUT or 3)
.TP
.B \-\-profile
device profile JSON (the shared profiles/ schema; scrape\-marked entries
feed the metric registers) (default: config, $SCRAPER_PROFILE or the
bundled sun2000 profile)
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-spec
metrics spec JSON: metric name \-> {help, type, profile?} (default:
config, $SCRAPER_METRICS_SPEC or the bundled metrics.json)
.TP
.BI \-\-pv\-register " N"
PV power register, signed I32 watts (default: config,
$SCRAPER_PV_REGISTER, the profile or 32064)
.TP
.BI \-\-grid\-register " N"
grid power register, signed I32 watts (default: config,
$SCRAPER_GRID_REGISTER or 37113)
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " N"
PV register multiplier (default: config, $SCRAPER_SCALE or 1)
.TP
.BI \-\-grid\-scale " N"
grid register multiplier (default: config, $SCRAPER_GRID_SCALE or 1)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-kwp " N"
maximum PV array kWp (default: config, $SCRAPER_MAX_KWP or 6; 0 = no
checking)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-grid\-kw " N"
maximum grid kW, either direction (default: config, $SCRAPER_MAX_GRID_KW
or 12; 0 = no checking)
.TP
.B \-\-battery
enable battery support (default: config, $SCRAPER_BATTERY or off)
.TP
.BI \-\-battery\-register " N"
battery power register, signed I32 watts, +charging (default: config,
$SCRAPER_BATTERY_REGISTER or 37001)
.TP
.BI \-\-battery\-soc\-register " N"
battery SoC register, U16 percent*10 (default: config,
$SCRAPER_BATTERY_SOC_REGISTER or 37004)
.TP
.B \-\-grid\-positive\-import
grid register positive when importing (default: config,
$SCRAPER_GRID_POSITIVE_IMPORT or positive = export)
.TP
.B \-\-listen
listen address HOST:PORT (default: config, $SCRAPER_LISTEN or
127.0.0.1:9350)
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " N"
seconds between polls (default: config, $SCRAPER_INTERVAL or 10)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-clients " N"
maximum concurrent HTTP clients; extras get an immediate 503 (default:
config, $SCRAPER_MAX_CLIENTS or 64; 0 = unlimited)
.TP
.BI \-\-client\-timeout " N"
seconds an idle keep\-alive HTTP client is kept before being kicked
(default: config, $SCRAPER_CLIENT_TIMEOUT or 300; 0 = off)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-conn\-per\-ip " N"
maximum concurrent HTTP connections from one peer IP; extras get an
immediate 503 (default: config, $SCRAPER_MAX_CONN_PER_IP or 0 = no
per\-IP limit)
.TP
.B \-\-local\-time
log timestamps in the system time zone instead of UTC (default: off)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
JSON\-lines control server target: unix socket path (default:
/tmp/modbus\-scraper\-<listen\-port>.socket) or TCP port number on
127.0.0.1 (e.g. 15599); 0 = off. Talk to it with scraper_ctl.py
(default: config, $SCRAPER_CONTROL_PORT)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
require a token on control connections: the client authenticates with
{"cmd": "auth", "token": ...}; over the unix socket a trusted peer
(root, the daemon's own user or \-\-control\-trust\-uids — SO_PEERCRED)
skips the token (default: config, $SCRAPER_CONTROL_TOKEN or none)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token\-file
the control token from a file (the first line; e.g. a systemd
LoadCredential or a key file; must be owner\-only 0600) — takes the
place of \-\-control\-token; giving both is an error (env
SCRAPER_CONTROL_TOKEN_FILE)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-trust\-uids
extra peer uids the unix control socket trusts without the token
(SO_PEERCRED — a local systemd unit speaks without the secret); root and
the daemon's own user are always trusted (default: config,
$SCRAPER_CONTROL_TRUST_UIDS or none)
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
SCR audit trail: a file path or \- for stdout (the docker/journald way);
default: the XDG state home (~/.local/state/modbus\-scraper/audit.log)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size in MB, keeping 3 backups; 0 = no size
rotation (default 10.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the SCR audit trail (default: off)
.TP
.B \-\-log\-access
log every HTTP request at INFO (default: config, $SCRAPER_LOG_ACCESS or
quiet)
.TP
.B \-\-auth\-token
require Authorization: Bearer <token> on all requests (default: config,
$SCRAPER_AUTH_TOKEN or disabled)
.TP
.B \-\-auth\-token\-file
read the bearer token from this file instead (single line, trimmed;
re\-read on every SIGHUP — rotate by rewriting the file and reloading;
must be owner\-only 0600); mutually exclusive with \-\-auth\-token
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level
log level (default: config, $SCRAPER_LOG_LEVEL or INFO)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
validate the configuration, print the effective settings and exit
(nothing is bound or connected) (default: off)


.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
re-read the config file (and the auth token file) and apply what is live
(the same path as the control server's request reload); a broken config
keeps the previous settings.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
graceful shutdown.

.SH CONTROL
The control server speaks JSON lines ({"cmd": "..."} ->
{"status": "ok|err|bye", "text": "..."}; TCP requires the token when
configured and refuses to start without one). Commands:
\fBset\fR/\fBunset\fR/\fBshow\fR/\fBhelp\fR (the settings: interval,
timeout, max-clients, client-timeout, max-conn-per-ip, log-access,
log-level), \fBshow status\fR, \fBshow connections\fR (the live HTTP
clients), \fBshow settings\fR, \fBshow version\fR, \fBpoll now\fR,
\fBinspect\fR, \fBrequest reload\fR, \fBrestart\fR, \fBshutdown\fR,
\fBquit\fR. See
.BR modbus-scraper-ctl (1)
and
.BR modbus-scraper-cli (1).

.SH SECURITY
The scraper reads an open Modbus device (no auth, no TLS — the inverter's
network isolation is the boundary) and serves /metrics: bind loopback by
default, set the bearer token when it must serve beyond loopback (a
non-loopback token-less start is refused, F13), and keep the connection
caps on. The control surface is loopback-only (TCP) or a 0600 unix socket;
a TCP control port without a token refuses to start (F5); with a token the
wire is signed and the commands/replies verify end to end. The audit trail
(default in the XDG state home, prefix SCR) records the control commands,
the auth failures, the reloads and the shutdowns.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/modbus-scraper-<listen-port>.socket
the default control socket.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/modbus-scraper/audit.log
the default audit trail.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-scraper-ctl (1),
.BR modbus-scraper-cli (1),
.BR modbus-cache (1),
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1)
.PP
scrape/README.md in the suite checkout \(em the full documentation.
